  "description": "1 x Oak (applicants ref. T1) - Reduce crown height and lateral spread back to previous pruning points by approximately 2 metres. Remove all dead wood for safety. Works proposed to improve light levels to the property and as part of routine tree maintenance. Standing in T10 of Tree Preservation Order.\r\r1 x Oak (applicants ref. T2) - Reduce crown height by approximately 2 metres and lateral spread by approximately 3 metres. The tree has a very large crown with substantial limbs encroaching over the roadside, public footpath, and garden area. Remove major dead wood for safety. Works proposed as part of general tree maintenance and to manage overhang onto the public highway. Standing in T5 of Tree Preservation Order.\r\r1 x Oak (applicants ref. T3) - Reduce crown height and lateral spread by approximately 2 metres. Approximately half of the crown overhangs the public footpath and roadside. Remove major dead wood to reduce risk and for public safety. Works proposed as part of routine tree maintenance. Standing in T3 of Tree Preservation.\r\r1 x Horse Chestnut (applicants ref. T4) - Reduce crown height by approximately 1.5 metres and lateral spread by approximately 2 metres. The tree is leaning towards a busy main road and roundabout. Remove major dead wood for safety. Works proposed to reduce risk and as part of general tree maintenance. Stanfding in T4 of Tree Preservation Order."
